shortname         = "-gw"
short_description = "read-only git (fetch/pull allowed)"
full_description  = "Deny every git action that writes — staging, committing, pushing, merges, rebases, resets, checkouts and restores, branch/tag/stash/config/remote changes, and the plumbing beneath them — so git stays read-only, except that fetching and pulling (fetch, pull, remote update, lfs fetch/pull) stay allowed: status, log, diff, show, blame, grep and the other reading commands run too. Nested under <-gpush>, which it requires and goes beyond (<-gpush> alone still allows local commits); weaker than <-git>, which denies git entirely. Fails closed where a command's prefix cannot tell reading from writing: branch, tag, stash, config, worktree, notes, reflog and submodule are denied whole (read them through for-each-ref, show-branch, log -g or .git/config), and so is any global option before the subcommand (`git -C dir …`, `git -c …` — cd first). Bash-pattern-level only: an env prefix (`GIT_DIR=x git commit`), an absolute path, env/command/eval, a git alias (`git ci`), and sibling binaries that write repositories (gh, glab — installed exactly when their credentials are staged) are separate spellings and NOT covered."
stance            = "deny"
